**Claim 1.**

A fuel cell system control apparatus, comprising:

an anode gas circulation flow rate control unit configured to control a circulation flow rate of anode gas circulating through an anode system of a fuel cell stack;

a wet/dry state detecting unit configured to detect a wet/dry state of the fuel cell stack;

a priority setting unit configured to set, based on the wet/dry state detected by the wet/dry state detecting unit, a priority between a wet/dry state control of the fuel cell stack and an anode gas circulation flow rate control performed by the anode gas circulation flow rate control unit;

an anode gas circulation flow rate limiting unit configured to limit the circulation flow rate of the anode gas in accordance with the priority set by the priority setting unit; and

a control quantity compensating unit configured to compensate a control quantity of the anode gas circulation flow rate control unit based on a limitation imposed by the anode gas circulation flow rate limiting unit,

wherein the anode gas circulation flow rate control unit controls the circulation flow rate of the anode gas in accordance with the control quantity compensated by the control quantity compensating unit.
